Problem 4.4
Suppose the running time T(n) of an algorithm is
bounded by a standard recurrence with T(n) <= 5 · T(n/3)+O(n).
Which of the following is the smallest correct upper bound on the
asymptotic running time of the algorithm?

a) O(n^log5 3)
b) O(n log n)
c) O(n^log3 5)
d) O(n^5/3)
e) O(n^2)
f) O(n^2.59)

answer:
ok so we have
a = 5
b = 3
and d = 1

a = b^2
5 = 3^1
5 = 3
5 > 3

5 . (n/3) + n
so this is the a wins case, spawns more subproblem/branch
aka leaves win scenario, so most work will be done on the leaves level
now to analyze

level 0 -> c . n
level 1 -> 5c . (n/3)^1 = 5/3 cn
level 2 -> 25c . (n/9) = (5/3)^2 cn
... etc

total work = work per level . total number of levels
work per level = c . n
number of levels (tree height) = log3 n (size drops by factor of 3) each level

branches = a = 5 times at each level
height = log 3 n
a^logb n = n^log b a
the answer is c

